  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As of the latest update, for various users, the Quest client has ceased to properly function. Namely, login is intermittent, sometimes taking up to at least 5 minutes, or more, then freezes when attempting to load a world. Sometimes, this may result in a crash, but when the freeze \"resolves\" after a \"few\" minutes, it then shows a world load progress with a size of 0 bytes, and does not progress further. On other networks, login may be speedy and successful, but this will result in the user being thrown into a \"black void\" with no controls, menu, or feedback, rather than the world that was supposed to be loaded. Only way of exit is by forcefully closing the app via the Quest universal menu. Standard troubleshooting does not remedy these issues, and these issues only began occurring within approx. the last month with a recent batch of updates.\n\nThe Quest client is, for all intents and purposes, unusable for those who encounter this issue. Support only offers basic troubleshooting remedies for the Quest client.\n\nI have video of the issue in action, posted to #user-support in the official discord.",
